#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Luka and took the pilgrims home across the sea."
msgstr "Vous avez trouvé Luka et ramené les pèlerins chez eux, de l'autre côté de la mer."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "In Ragusa, the bells ring for them."
msgstr "À Raguse, les cloches sonnent pour eux."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! The corsairs of Ulcinj took all our olive oil."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines} ! Les corsaires d'Ulcinj ont pris toute notre huile d'olive."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "We traded it for the winter, and now we have nothing."
msgstr "Nous voulions l'échanger pour l'hiver, et maintenant nous n'avons plus rien."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nobody fights them. Go and ask what they want for it!"
msgstr "Personne ne se bat contre eux. Allez leur demander ce qu'ils veulent en échange !"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil for oil? No, no. My sail is torn to rags."
msgstr "De l'huile contre de l'huile ? Non, non. Ma voile est en lambeaux."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a new sail, and you get your oil back."
msgstr "Apportez-moi une voile neuve, et vous récupérez votre huile."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The sailmaker of Durrës makes the best sails."
msgstr "Le maître voilier de Durrës fait les meilleures voiles."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A new sail! Fine work. Here is your oil, captain."
msgstr ""
"Une voile neuve ! Du beau travail. Voici votre huile, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And tell the Aga that Crooked Mast is not his friend."
msgstr "Et dites à l'Aga que Mât-Tordu n'est pas son ami."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sail? Gladly, but my cough is so bad, I can not work."
msgstr "Une voile ? Avec plaisir, mais je tousse si fort que je ne peux pas travailler."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Only the honey of Vlorë helps."
msgstr "Seul le miel de Vlorë peut m'aider."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a jar of honey!"
msgstr "Apportez-moi un pot de miel !"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey from Vlorë! My cough is gone already."
msgstr "Du miel de Vlorë ! Ma toux est déjà partie."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the sail. The finest in the Adriatic!"
msgstr "Voici la voile. La plus belle de l'Adriatique !"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey? My bees made plenty."
msgstr "Du miel ? Mes abeilles en ont fait plein."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my cheese. Do you have salt on board?"
msgstr "Mais il me faut du sel pour mon fromage. Avez-vous du sel à bord ?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Just what I needed."
msgstr "Du sel ! Juste ce qu'il me fallait."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is a jar of my best honey."
msgstr "Voici un pot de mon meilleur miel."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the olive oil home to {port}."
msgstr "Ramenez l'huile d'olive {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our oil! Now we have enough for the winter."
msgstr "Notre huile ! Maintenant, nous en avons assez pour l'hiver."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast sent a message, too:"
msgstr "Mât-Tordu a aussi envoyé un message :"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"The Aga's scribe sails south with a heavy book. Watch out for him!\""
msgstr "« Le scribe de l'Aga file vers le sud avec un gros livre. Méfiez-vous de lui ! »"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Corsairs of Ulcinj"
msgstr "Les corsaires d'Ulcinj"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The corsairs took the villages' olive oil. Find out what they want, and trade it back."
msgstr ""
"Les corsaires ont pris l'huile d'olive des villages. Découvrez ce qu'ils veulent, et récupérez-la "
"par des échanges."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The olive trees of the Adriatic grow very old: near Bar in Montenegro stands an olive tree which "
"is said to be more than two thousand years old."
msgstr ""
"Les oliviers de l'Adriatique deviennent très vieux : près de Bar, au Monténégro, pousse un olivier"
" qui aurait plus de deux mille ans."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oil is home!"
msgstr "L'huile est rentrée !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Not a single shot was fired: a sail, a jar of honey and a sack of salt did it."
msgstr "Pas un seul coup de feu : une voile, un pot de miel et un sac de sel ont suffi."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Even the corsair captain is your friend now."
msgstr "Même le capitaine corsaire est votre ami maintenant."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax!"
msgstr "{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, l'Aga veut les oranges de Parga comme impôt !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eleni of Parga hid the harvest from his men."
msgstr "Eleni de Parga a caché la récolte à ses hommes."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Help her get the oranges to the market of Corfu, so that the money stays with the people."
msgstr "Aidez-la à porter les oranges au marché de Corfou, pour que l'argent reste aux gens."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges are ripe, but the Aga's men broke all my baskets."
msgstr "Les oranges sont mûres, mais les hommes de l'Aga ont cassé tous mes paniers."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me baskets! Ilir of Vlorë weaves the best ones."
msgstr "Apportez-moi des paniers ! Ilir de Vlorë tresse les meilleurs."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine baskets! Here are the oranges, captain."
msgstr "De beaux paniers ! Voici les oranges, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Smell them: the sun of Parga is inside."
msgstr "Sentez-les : le soleil de Parga est dedans."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave baskets from the reeds of the lagoon."
msgstr "Je tresse des paniers avec les roseaux de la lagune."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But my boat lost its rope. Spiros in Corfu has ropes!"
msgstr "Mais mon bateau a perdu sa corde. Spiros, à Corfou, a des cordes !"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good rope! Here are my baskets."
msgstr "Une bonne corde ! Voici mes paniers."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope for Ilir? The harbour of Corfu has ropes for everybody."
msgstr "Une corde pour Ilir ? Le port de Corfou a des cordes pour tout le monde."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this one, captain."
msgstr "Prenez celle-ci, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the oranges to the market of {port}."
msgstr "Apportez les oranges au marché, {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oranges from Parga! The whole market smells of them."
msgstr "Des oranges de Parga ! Tout le marché sent l'orange."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The money goes to the people of Parga, not to the Aga."
msgstr "L'argent va aux gens de Parga, pas à l'Aga."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every orange was sold, and Parga keeps its money."
msgstr "Toutes les oranges sont vendues, et Parga garde son argent."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga gets only the peels!"
msgstr "L'Aga n'a que les épluchures !"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Oranges of Parga"
msgstr "Les oranges de Parga"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax. Trade your way to baskets and bring the oranges to "
"the market of Corfu."
msgstr ""
"L'Aga veut les oranges de Parga comme impôt. Échangez jusqu'à obtenir des paniers et portez les "
"oranges au marché de Corfou."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Parga was a little Venetian town on the Greek coast for almost 400 years, with Ottoman lands all "
"around it, and it was often raided by its neighbours."
msgstr ""
"Parga a été une petite ville vénitienne sur la côte grecque pendant presque 400 ans, entourée de "
"terres ottomanes, et ses voisins l'attaquaient souvent."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sweet oranges for Corfu!"
msgstr "De douces oranges pour Corfou !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges reached the market, and the money stayed in Parga."
msgstr "Les oranges sont arrivées au marché, et l'argent est resté à Parga."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope, a basket and a lot of sailing did it."
msgstr "Une corde, un panier et beaucoup de navigation ont suffi."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the warning of Crooked Mast came true!"
msgstr "{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, l'avertissement de Mât-Tordu s'est réalisé !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe was here with a heavy book: the ledger of the double taxes."
msgstr "Le scribe de l'Aga était ici avec un gros livre : le registre des doubles impôts."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "With it, we can prove everything. But he fled in a hurry. Chase him!"
msgstr "Avec lui, nous pouvons tout prouver. Mais il s'est enfui en vitesse. Poursuivez-le !"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The scribe had {hallmark}."
msgstr "Le scribe avait {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Aga's scribe with a heavy book?"
msgstr "Avez-vous vu le scribe de l'Aga avec un gros livre ?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, hiding among the people of the harbour! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Il est ici, caché parmi les gens du port ! Mais lequel est-ce ?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the Aga's scribe?"
msgstr "Lequel est le scribe de l'Aga ?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the scribe! Remember all four things you learned."
msgstr "Non, ce n'est pas le scribe ! Souvenez-vous des quatre choses que vous avez apprises."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Alright, alright! Here is the ledger. I only wrote what the Aga told me!\""
msgstr "« Bon, d'accord ! Voici le registre. Je n'ai écrit que ce que l'Aga m'a dit ! »"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"I will tell the truth before the judge, I promise.\""
msgstr "« Je dirai la vérité devant le juge, promis. »"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger proves it: the Aga took every tax twice!"
msgstr "Le registre le prouve : l'Aga a pris chaque impôt deux fois !"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Forged Ledger"
msgstr "Le registre truqué"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe flees with the ledger of the double taxes. Chase him along the coast!"
msgstr ""
"Le scribe de l'Aga s'enfuit avec le registre des doubles impôts. Poursuivez-le le long de la "
"côte !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Spectacles were made in Venice from about 1300 on; the glassmakers of Murano were so precious that"
" they were not allowed to leave the republic."
msgstr ""
"On fabriquait des lunettes à Venise dès 1300 environ ; les verriers de Murano étaient si précieux "
"qu'ils n'avaient pas le droit de quitter la république."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger is yours!"
msgstr "Le registre est à vous !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You chased the scribe along the whole coast and found him."
msgstr "Vous avez poursuivi le scribe tout le long de la côte et vous l'avez trouvé."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the crew holds the proof of the double taxes."
msgstr "Maintenant, l'équipage a la preuve des doubles impôts."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, I must confess something."
msgstr "{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, je dois vous avouer quelque chose."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I wrote the list of the villages in the old Glagolitic letters, so that the Aga could not read it."
msgstr ""
"J'ai écrit la liste des villages avec les vieilles lettres glagolitiques, pour que l'Aga ne puisse"
" pas la lire."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now I can not read it either! Find a priest who knows the old letters."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant, moi non plus, je ne peux pas la lire ! Trouvez un prêtre qui connaît les vieilles "
"lettres."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The priest has {hallmark}."
msgstr "Le prêtre a {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen a priest who knows the old letters?"
msgstr "Avez-vous vu un prêtre qui connaît les vieilles lettres ?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur is here, at the market! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Don Grgur est ici, au marché ! Mais lequel est-ce ?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Don Grgur? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Lequel est don Grgur ? Souvenez-vous de ce que les gens vous ont dit !"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not him! Think of all three things you learned."
msgstr "Non, ce n'est pas lui ! Pensez aux trois choses que vous avez apprises."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Yes, I read the old letters. Let me see... every village, and every ducat!\""
msgstr "« Oui, je lis les vieilles lettres. Voyons... chaque village, et chaque ducat ! »"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the list back to the scribe in {port}."
msgstr "Rapportez la liste au scribe, {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every village and every ducat, written clearly at last!"
msgstr "Chaque village et chaque ducat, enfin écrits clairement !"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge can give back every coin."
msgstr "Maintenant, le juge peut rendre chaque pièce."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is ready for the judge."
msgstr "La liste est prête pour le juge."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will never write in a secret script again!"
msgstr "Je n'écrirai plus jamais en écriture secrète !"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Secret Script"
msgstr "L'écriture secrète"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The list of the villages is written in old Glagolitic letters. Find a priest who can read it."
msgstr ""
"La liste des villages est écrite en vieilles lettres glagolitiques. Trouvez un prêtre qui sait la "
"lire."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Glagolitic is the oldest known Slavic alphabet. On the islands of Kvarner, like Krk, and on the "
"islands near Zadar, Croatian priests and scribes kept writing in it for centuries."
msgstr ""
"Le glagolitique est le plus ancien alphabet slave connu. Sur les îles du Kvarner, comme Krk, et "
"sur les îles près de Zadar, des prêtres et des scribes croates ont continué à l'écrire pendant des"
" siècles."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is read!"
msgstr "La liste est lue !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur read the old letters for you."
msgstr "Don Grgur a lu les vieilles lettres pour vous."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge will know every village and every ducat."
msgstr "Maintenant, le juge connaîtra chaque village et chaque ducat."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the judge wants to hear witnesses, not only the ledger."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, le juge veut entendre des témoins, pas seulement le "
"registre."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast in Ulcinj, Mustafa in Castelnuovo and Jele in Kotor saw what the Aga's men did."
msgstr ""
"Mât-Tordu à Ulcinj, Mustafa à Castelnuovo et Jele à Kotor ont vu ce qu'ont fait les hommes de "
"l'Aga."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring all three to Corfu, where the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "Amenez-les tous les trois à Corfou, où commence le voyage vers le juge !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Me, a witness? Ha! Fine."
