#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the friars on the islet of Košljun see every boat in their bay."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, les moines de l'îlot de Košljun voient chaque bateau de "
"leur baie."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They sent word: they saw the false boats! Ask Brother Ambroz on Krk."
msgstr "Ils nous ont prévenus : ils ont vu les faux bateaux ! Demandez à frère Ambroz, à Krk."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Talk to Brother Ambroz on {port}."
msgstr "Parlez à frère Ambroz, {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Peace be with you, captain. Yes, we saw boats with new white sails."
msgstr ""
"La paix soit avec vous, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}. Oui, nous avons vu des bateaux aux "
"voiles blanches neuves."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They sailed south between the islands. Ask in the towns!"
msgstr "Ils sont partis vers le sud entre les îles. Demandez dans les villes !"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen boats with brand-new white sails?"
msgstr "Avez-vous vu des bateaux aux voiles blanches toutes neuves ?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They hide close by. Brother Ambroz left you a letter about it."
msgstr "Ils se cachent tout près. Frère Ambroz vous a laissé une lettre à ce sujet."

#. what a judge says before the questions, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Brother Ambroz wrote you a riddle, captain."
msgstr "Frère Ambroz vous a écrit une devinette, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}."

#. what a judge says before the questions, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Answer me, and you will know where the false boats hide.\""
msgstr "« Répondez-moi, et vous saurez où se cachent les faux bateaux. »"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hmm, no. Read the riddle again, captain."
msgstr "Hmm, non. Relisez la devinette, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cove behind Osor! But the false boats have left it."
msgstr "La crique derrière Osor ! Mais les faux bateaux l'ont quittée."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Their things are still there, I bet."
msgstr "Leurs affaires sont sûrement encore là."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The friars of Košljun watch the sea day and night."
msgstr "Les moines de Košljun surveillent la mer jour et nuit."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Go with God, captain, and look in that cove!"
msgstr "Allez avec Dieu, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}, et fouillez cette crique !"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Friars of Košljun"
msgstr "Les moines de Košljun"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The friars on their islet saw where the false boats hide. Follow their word through the islands."
msgstr ""
"Depuis leur îlot, les moines ont vu où se cachent les faux bateaux. Suivez leurs indications à "
"travers les îles."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Franciscan friars have lived on the islet of Košljun near Krk since 1447. They still keep old "
"books and maps there."
msgstr ""
"Des moines franciscains vivent sur l'îlot de Košljun, près de Krk, depuis 1447. Ils y gardent "
"encore de vieux livres et de vieilles cartes."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The hideout is found!"
msgstr "La cachette est trouvée !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The riddle of Brother Ambroz led you to the cove behind Osor."
msgstr ""
"La devinette de frère Ambroz {crew|vous a mené|vous a menée|vous a menés|vous a menées} à la "
"crique derrière Osor."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/30_friars_of_kosljun/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The false uskoks are gone, but their hideout is not."
msgstr "Les faux uscoques sont partis, mais leur cachette est toujours là."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uskok coats from the cove, all brand-new!"
msgstr "Des manteaux d'uscoques de la crique, tout neufs !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them, captain."
msgstr "Prenez-les, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flags with the uskok sign, never touched by the wind."
msgstr "Des drapeaux avec le signe des uscoques, que le vent n'a jamais touchés."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They washed up below my quarry."
msgstr "La mer les a rejetés au pied de ma carrière."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bales of Venetian cloth, hidden in the cave of my sheep!"
msgstr "Des ballots de tissu vénitien, cachés dans la grotte de mes moutons !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "This is the stolen cargo."
msgstr "C'est la cargaison volée."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the cove is empty, but the false uskoks left in a hurry."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, la crique est vide, mais les faux uscoques sont partis en "
"vitesse."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The people of the islands found their things. Collect them all!"
msgstr "Les gens des îles ont trouvé leurs affaires. Rassemblez-les toutes !"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Collect {count} more {count|thing|things} from the hideout."
msgstr "Encore {count} {count|objet|objets} de la cachette à rassembler."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring everything to Juraj in {port}."
msgstr "Apportez tout à Juraj, {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look at these coats! Not one of us ever wore them."
msgstr "Regardez ces manteaux ! Aucun de nous ne les a jamais portés."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And false flags! They were sewn last month."
msgstr "Et de faux drapeaux ! Ils ont été cousus le mois dernier."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cloth of the Venetian ships! We will give it back."
msgstr "Le tissu des navires vénitiens ! Nous allons le rendre."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Costumes, flags and the stolen cloth: a whole chest of proof!"
msgstr "Des déguisements, des drapeaux et le tissu volé : tout un coffre de preuves !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now we only need to know who paid for it all."
msgstr "Il ne reste plus qu'à savoir qui a payé tout ça."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Hidden Cove"
msgstr "La crique cachée"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The hideout of the false uskoks is empty. Collect what they left behind on the islands."
msgstr "La cachette des faux uscoques est vide. Rassemblez ce qu'ils ont laissé sur les îles."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The canal of Osor was dug already in Roman times. Boats still sail through it between Cres and "
"Lošinj, under a bridge which swings aside."
msgstr ""
"Le canal d'Osor a été creusé dès l'époque romaine. Les bateaux y passent encore entre Cres et "
"Lošinj, sous un pont qui pivote."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The proofs are in Senj!"
msgstr "Les preuves sont à Senj !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You collected the costumes, the flags and the stolen cloth."
msgstr "Vous avez rassemblé les déguisements, les drapeaux et le tissu volé."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/31_hidden_cove/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Juraj keeps them safe in the Nehaj fortress."
msgstr "Juraj les garde en sûreté dans la forteresse de Nehaj."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Baron's steward was here, asking about you!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, l'intendant du baron est venu ici, et il a posé des "
"questions sur vous !"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He carries the payroll: the list of the men paid to play uskoks."
msgstr "Il porte la liste de paie : la liste des hommes payés pour jouer aux uscoques."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He fled by boat. Chase him!"
msgstr "Il s'est enfui en bateau. Poursuivez-le !"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The steward had {hallmark}."
msgstr "L'intendant avait {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Baron's steward?"
msgstr "Avez-vous vu l'intendant du baron ?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the Baron's steward?"
msgstr "Lequel est l'intendant du baron ?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the steward! Remember all four things you learned."
msgstr "Non, ce n'est pas l'intendant ! Souvenez-vous des quatre choses que vous avez apprises."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Alright! Here is the payroll. The Baron signed every page.\""
msgstr "« D'accord ! Voici la liste de paie. Le baron a signé chaque page. »"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"The Baron never even paid me!\""
msgstr "« Le baron ne m'a même jamais payé ! »"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"I will tell the Archduke's commissioner everything.\""
msgstr "« Je dirai tout au commissaire de l'archiduc. »"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Steward's Ledger"
msgstr "La liste de l'intendant"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Baron's steward flees with the payroll of the false uskoks. Chase him!"
msgstr "L'intendant du baron s'enfuit avec la liste de paie des faux uscoques. Poursuivez-le !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Around 1600, Rijeka and Trieste belonged to the Archduke of Inner Austria, a Habsburg who ruled "
"from the town of Graz."
msgstr ""
"Vers 1600, Rijeka et Trieste appartenaient à l'archiduc d'Autriche intérieure, un Habsbourg qui "
"régnait depuis la ville de Graz."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The payroll is yours!"
msgstr "La liste de paie est à vous !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You chased the steward through Kvarner and Istria."
msgstr "Vous avez poursuivi l'intendant à travers le Kvarner et l'Istrie."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "His payroll shows who paid the false uskoks: Baron Isengrim."
msgstr "Sa liste de paie montre qui a payé les faux uscoques : le baron Ysengrin."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Archduke sent a commissioner to Trieste."
msgstr "{crew|Capitaine|Capitaine|Capitaines}, l'archiduc a envoyé un commissaire à Trieste."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He will judge the Baron, but Venice must send an envoy, too."
msgstr "Il jugera le baron, mais il faut aussi un envoyé de Venise."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Get his safe-conduct for the envoy, and carry it to Venice!"
msgstr "Obtenez son sauf-conduit pour l'envoyé, et portez-le à Venise !"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Get the safe-conduct of the commissioner in {port}."
msgstr "Obtenez le sauf-conduit du commissaire, {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Baron has shamed the Archduke's name."
msgstr "Le baron a déshonoré le nom de l'archiduc."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "With this letter, the envoy of Venice may come safely to Rijeka."
msgstr "Avec cette lettre, l'envoyé de Venise peut venir à Rijeka en toute sécurité."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the safe-conduct to the envoy in {port}."
msgstr "Apportez le sauf-conduit à l'envoyé, {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A safe-conduct of the Archduke, for a Venetian? Times change!"
msgstr "Un sauf-conduit de l'archiduc, pour un Vénitien ? Les temps changent !"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will sail to Rijeka at once."
msgstr "Je pars tout de suite pour Rijeka."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The lion of St. Mark and the eagle of the Habsburgs at one table."
msgstr "Le lion de saint Marc et l'aigle des Habsbourg à la même table."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Peace is worth a voyage, captain!"
msgstr "La paix vaut bien un voyage, {crew|capitaine|capitaine|capitaines} !"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Two Flags"
msgstr "Deux drapeaux"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Carry the commissioner's safe-conduct from Trieste to the envoy in Venice. Mind both patrols!"
msgstr ""
"Portez le sauf-conduit du commissaire de Trieste à l'envoyé de Venise. Attention aux deux "
"patrouilles !"

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A safe-conduct was a letter which promised a traveller that nobody would stop or harm him, even in"
" the land of another ruler."
msgstr ""
"Un sauf-conduit était une lettre qui promettait à un voyageur que personne ne l'arrêterait ni ne "
"lui ferait de mal, même sur les terres d'un autre souverain."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The envoy is coming!"
msgstr "L'envoyé arrive !"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You carried the safe-conduct past the patrols of two powers."
msgstr "Vous avez fait passer le sauf-conduit entre les patrouilles de deux puissances."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/33_two_flags/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The envoy of Venice sails to Rijeka."
msgstr "L'envoyé de Venise part pour Rijeka."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/34_through_the_bura/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I'll come, bura or no bura!"
